  "body": "Adds a **Walk** option to cardio logging — pace and duration, no intervals.\n\n## A walk is a treadmill workout, not a new activity\n\nIt is done on the treadmill, so it shares the treadmill activity, color and history lane. It differs from the interval templates only in that its single `walk` interval (the type those templates already use) is entered per session instead of being fixed.\n\n## The template document is the default\n\nMirrors how a strength exercise's default lives on the exercise definition. The walk is a real `cardio-template` (`steady-walk`, `steady: true`) created by migration 006, so:\n\n- Selecting **Walk** prefills the saved pace and duration.\n- Ticking **\"This is the new default\"** writes the entered values back to the template via the existing admin `PUT /api/cardio-templates/:templateId` — no new endpoint.\n- The promotion runs *before* the session is logged and aborts the log if it fails, so the default and the log can never disagree. Same behavior as the strength flow.\n\nMigration 006 is re-runnable and deliberately preserves whatever intervals the document already holds, so re-applying can never reset a default set from the app.\n\n## Display\n\nA logged treadmill session with one interval is a steady one: the detail view shows a **Speed** metric instead of a one-row Intervals list, and the summary line reads `3.4 mph` instead of `0 jog intervals, 32 min`.\n\n## Verification\n\nRun against the live database from the dev server:\n\n- Dry-run: 1 pending migration, `create: 2`, safe to retry.\n- Walk prefilled 3.2/30 from the template; logged 3.6/40 with the box ticked → template default became 3.6/40 and the next form load prefilled it.\n- Logged 2.9/15 with the box unticked → default stayed 3.6/40.\n- Test sessions and the hand-created template were deleted afterwards; migration 006 has since been applied for real, so the Walk template now exists in the database and the runner will skip it at deploy.\n- Frontend lint and build pass; backend tests pass (7/7).",
